From 9e690ad0a80cd7e0ae9a9b61a84bf0876ffb0568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:14:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] msearch --diag-first: d-first search with a posting
 index and a top-label root

For sums with at least --diag-first-min-n vectors (default 3000), msearch
searches V_d = {v : |v & d| = 1} for every vector d of the sum (src/c/
dfirst.c): every (square, SP traversal) pair once, every magic square
twice. V_d comes from a number -> vector posting index. Every square of
V_d contains all of d, so d's numbers get the top labels and only the
first rows through the rarest of them are roots: 0.64-0.70x the time of
the plain V_d root at the same d (--d-plain-root keeps it; it reproduces
bin/dsearch's nodes).

Chunks with checkpoint records (--d-chunk, --d-range), d sampling
(--d-stride/--d-offset) with estimates and standard errors, a per-d log,
and a calibration stream (--calib-r1-stride: r1-sampled plain search).
The r1 sampling of cx/profile is now in search_opts_t, stratified as an
option (--r1-stride, --r1-strata, --r1-log, SAMPLE_* env in msearch and
bench); the default root loop is unchanged (same nodes and hashes).

Measured against stratified r1-sampled plain search (relSE <= 9%), d-first
costs 0.27-0.37x per sum at N = 15-23k (geometric mean 0.31; the plain
root 0.47), 0.56-0.61x at 6-8k and 0.86x at 4.1k; crossover N ~ 3000
(research/ideas.md). Tests: fuzz_arrange --dfirst (brute force over
random diagonal sets, a planted diagonal pair), msearch on 849 / 16 5 4 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
